<title>BAHRAIN: Gulf International Bank H1 net profit up 20 pct.</title>
<headline>Gulf International Bank H1 net profit up 20 pct.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to June 30, 1997</p>
<p>			    (U.S. million dollars)</p>
<p> Net profit		 52.7    vs    43.9</p>
<p> Operating income	 75.1    vs    65.0</p>
<p> Operating expenses     22.1    vs    21.0</p>
<p> Net operating income   53.0    vs    44.0</p>
<p> Provision		  10.0    vs     5.0</p>
<p> Shareholders' equity  705.3    vs   646.8</p>
<p> Assets		  9,038.7    vs 8,620.5</p>
<p>Full Name: Gulf International Bank B.S.C.</p>
<p>Note - The Bahrain-based bank is wholly owned by Kuwait-based Gulf Investment Corp, which in turn is held by the governments of Saudi Arabia, Bahrain, Oman, Qatar, the United Arab Emirates and Kuwait.</p>
<p>-- Bahrain newsroom 973-524424.</p>
</text>
